-- Conformance: a handler clause's parameter is a binder, held to the type the
-- operation is performed with (Chapter 7, Section 7.5.1).  Tests: E342 —
-- `throw(@String)` under `handle[Exn<Int>]` is refused: the value `throw`
-- passes is an Int, and a clause parameter binds it at the type it writes,
-- so that type must be the operation's parameter type or a supertype of it,
-- as a let binding's must be (#1896).  A `@Nat` or refined parameter over an
-- Int is checked where it binds (see ch07_exn_payload_guard), and an alias
-- of the operation's type stays accepted (see ch07_exn_param_alias).
public fn go(@Int -> @Int)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(pure)
{
  handle[Exn<Int>] {
    throw(@String) -> { 0 }
  } in {
    throw(@Int.0)
  }
}
